language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Sum the even-valued Fibonacci terms (starting 1, 2) that do not exceed four million.
find fib : matrix indexed by [int(1..33)] of int(1..10000000)
find res : int(0..10000000)

branching on [fib]

such that
$ the sequence starts with 1 and 2
fib[1] = 1,
fib[2] = 2,
$ each new term is the sum of the previous two terms
forAll i : int(3..33) . fib[i] = fib[i-1] + fib[i-2],
$ res is the sum of the even terms that do not exceed four million
res = (sum i : int(1..33) . toInt(fib[i] % 2 = 0 /\ fib[i] <= 4000000) * fib[i])
